<article class="env-remark" id="06JA">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06JA">Remark <span data-tag="06JA">9.4.5.5</span>.</a> In the situation of Theorem <a data-tag="06J9" href="/tag/06J9">9.4.5.4</a>, suppose that we are given a functor of $\infty $-categories $H: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\pm }$. Then: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
If $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-cocomplete, then $H$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary if and only if the functors $(G_{-} \circ H): \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}$ and $(G_{+} \circ H): \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$ are $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compactly generated, then $H$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compact if and only if the functors $G_{-} \circ H$ and $G_{+} \circ H$ are $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compact. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> The first assertion is a special case of Proposition <a data-tag="06AA" href="/tag/06AA">7.1.9.1</a>, and the second follows by combining Proposition <a data-tag="06AA" href="/tag/06AA">7.1.9.1</a> with the characterization of $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compact objects of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\pm }$ supplied by Theorem <a data-tag="06J9" href="/tag/06J9">9.4.5.4</a>. </p>
<p>Applying this observation in the special case where $H$ is the identity functor $\operatorname{id}_{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\pm } }$, we see that the functors $G_{-}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\pm } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}$ and $G_{+}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\pm } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$ are $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compact. </p>
</article>
